    %h3 What is Bedbug Reporter?
    %p
      Bedbug Reporter is a community map of bed bug sightings. Anyone can report where they found bed bugs, such as a hotel, apartment, dorm, or public space, and anyone can search a location before they travel, rent, or move.
    %p
      Every report includes an address, how severe the problem was, and whether it has been verified. Other users can rate reports up or down to help keep the information accurate.

    %h3 Where does the data come from?
    %p
      All reports are submitted by users. If you have seen bed bugs somewhere, please add a report so others can check before they stay.

    %h3 How do I submit a good report?
    %p
      Use the exact address, choose the severity honestly, and describe where you saw the bugs (for example, mattress seams or a couch). Please report only what you saw yourself.

    %h3 How can I help?
    %p
      %strong First:
      Add reports. The map is only as useful as the reports in it.
    %p
      %strong Second:
      Spread the word so more people check before they book or sign a lease.
    %p
      %strong Third:
      If you code, visit GitHub to report a bug, suggest an improvement, or contribute.

    %h3 Credits
    %p
      Bedbug Reporter is built on the open source
      %a{:href => "https://github.com/RefugeRestrooms/refugerestrooms"} Refuge Restrooms
      project.
